You sacrificed a Lawful Unicorn on a Lawful altar.  In other words, a
creature sacred to the god in question.  While you might normally be
able to convert an altar with a sacrifice, Unicorns are a special
case.  Sacrificing a unicorn on an altar of its own alignment gets the
god in question royally cheesed off at you, which results in the God
smacking you upside the head with some form of divine retribution. 
While Issek might not be your god, he's still *a* god, and thus is
powerful enough to remove your divine protection because you're just a
puny mortal.

